# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Two error messages in the app tell people to copy
# this file, so it needs to exist.
#
# Both values are read in lib/supabase.ts and are INLINED BY METRO AT BUILD TIME.
# There is no runtime lookup: changing project means rebuilding, not editing a setting.
# On Cloudflare Pages these go in the project's environment variables, because
# Cloudflare runs the build.
#
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> Data API

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# The anon key is PUBLIC by design and is meant to ship in the bundle. It carries no
# authority of its own — every row it can reach is decided by RLS and by the caller's
# JWT. The key that must never appear here, or anywhere in apps/, is the service_role
# key: it bypasses RLS entirely, which is how cross-tenant leaks actually happen
# (CLAUDE.md non-negotiable 3).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Optional. Absent means error reporting is simply off, which is the right behaviour
# for a local checkout. The DSN is public and safe to commit; the SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN
# that uploads source maps is not, and lives only in GitHub Actions secrets.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
